          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "अनुधावति — anudhāvati — \"runs after; chases\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "यामिकः चौरम् अनुधावति। yāmikaḥ cauram anudhāvati. The watchman runs after the thief."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (he …): सः चौरम् अनुधावितवान्, saḥ cauram anudhāvitavān."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "अनुधावति (anudhāvati) is built from anu, \"after\", and the root √dhāv, \"to run\", which also gives dhāvati, \"runs\"; MW gives anu-dhāv as to run after or pursue (MW)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
